# NetSec - its own strings.
#
# The daemon reads "Breach Network" / "Breach local network" on the breach
# screen, from keys NetSec owns rather than words borrowed from a vanilla
# record.
#
# WHY THIS IS THE SECOND ATTEMPT, AND WHAT IS DIFFERENT.
#
# v1.5.16 shipped an onscreens resource authored from a GUESSED CR2W schema.
# ArchiveXL logged loading the .xl, never logged merging the entries, and the
# log ended mid-merge - the game crashed, and it was reverted the same evening.
# Round-tripping it through WolvenKit had "verified" it, which proved only that
# WolvenKit could read back what WolvenKit had written.
#
# The difference this time is the template. This resource is built from the
# structure of a mod ALREADY INSTALLED AND WORKING on this machine -
# BlackChrome's phoenicia\blackchrome\translations\translation_strings.json,
# which ships named keys of exactly this kind and is referenced from TweakXL the
# same way. Its CR2W string table was compared against this one field by field.
#
# That comparison also named the old file's actual defect, which no amount of
# round-tripping could have shown: it declared the container type
# localizationPersistenceOnScreenEntries and never once declared
# localizationPersistenceOnScreenEntry, the per-entry type. The entries had no
# type to be. Vanilla's onscreens_final.json and BlackChrome's file both carry
# both names; the 1.5.16 archive carried only the first.
#
# Still not proof the runtime accepts it - only a run is that. The line to look
# for is ArchiveXL logging the merge of these entries and CONTINUING past it.
localization:
  onscreens:
    en-us: netsec\localization\en-us\onscreens\netsec.json
